import{_ as e,o as n,c as t,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const d=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 279 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Civilization Weight Analysis: Imbalance Between Tang Luo's Personal Weight and Civilizational Consensus","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 279 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Civilization Weight Analysis: Imbalance Between Tang Luo's Personal Weight and Civilizational Consensus","no":279,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Civilization Weight","Consensus Degree","Weight Imbalance","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["20-Anchor Structure and Hierarchy","29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System","49-Governance Framework and Power Checks"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0279_模块2-唐罗-文明权重分析.md","filePath":"en/0279_模块2-唐罗-文明权重分析.md"}`),s={name:"en/0279_模块2-唐罗-文明权重分析.md"};function a(r,i,l,g,u,c){return n(),t("div",null,[...i[0]||(i[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-279-tang-luo-decomposition-civilization-weight-analysis-imbalance-between-tang-luo-s-personal-weight-and-civilizational-consensus" tabindex="-1">Entry 279 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Civilization Weight Analysis: Imbalance Between Tang Luo&#39;s Personal Weight and Civilizational Consensus <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-279-tang-luo-decomposition-civilization-weight-analysis-imbalance-between-tang-luo-s-personal-weight-and-civilizational-consensus" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 279 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Civilization Weight Analysis: Imbalance Between Tang Luo&#39;s Personal Weight and Civilizational Consensus&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 29)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-one-person-represents-the-entire-civilization" tabindex="-1">Introduction: One person represents the entire civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-one-person-represents-the-entire-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: One person represents the entire civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the law-first axiom requires laws first; the collective ascension axiom requires Myriad Races co-construction. The Tang-Luo system&#39;s &quot;civilization weight&quot; is severely imbalanced — Tang Luo&#39;s personal weight is too high, civilization consensus degree too low. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, introducing &quot;civilization weight&quot; as a Heng Yuan Zhou term for structural analysis. Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Weight imbalance&#39;s energy-level waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Extreme consensus cost</strong>: because Tang Luo&#39;s weight is too high, every decision needs &quot;Tang Luo&#39;s nod.&quot; Tens of millions&#39; consensus rests on one person&#39;s judgment. Decision efficiency extremely low</li><li><strong>Dissent stifled</strong>: because Tang Luo&#39;s weight is too high, different opinions cannot enter decisions. Civilization decision-making is single-polarized, blind spots large</li><li><strong>Calibration missing</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s judgment bias has no calibration. Weight imbalance means &quot;if wrong, no one can say no&quot;</li></ul><p>Energy-level waste: <strong>civilization&#39;s collective wisdom is compressed into one person&#39;s personal judgment.</strong> A billion heads, ultimately only one person decides.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Single-polarized decisions</strong>: Tang Luo errs, the whole civilization errs with him. No error-correction mechanism</li><li><strong>Consensus cannot transmit</strong>: when Tang Luo is in office, consensus = Tang Luo&#39;s will. He retires, consensus vacuum</li><li><strong>Weight solidified</strong>: because Tang Luo&#39;s weight is too high, those around him lose the habit of independent judgment. Decades later, the whole civilization cannot think for itself</li></ol><p>Regression form: civilization increasingly depends on Tang Luo&#39;s brain, increasingly cannot use its own brain.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Monopolizing judgment right</strong>: Tang Luo takes &quot;right vs. wrong&quot; judgment right for himself. This is deprivation of all beings&#39; right to think</li><li><strong>Consensus outsourcing</strong>: all beings outsource &quot;what is good, what is right&quot; to Tang Luo. After outsourcing, all beings&#39; moral sense, judgment, responsibility all atrophy</li><li><strong>Weight is predation</strong>: personal weight too high is equivalent to declaring others&#39; weights near zero. This is weight-level predation</li></ul><p>By the Gu Chensha / Tang Luo judgment table standard: Tang Luo = <strong>enlightened predator</strong>, weight imbalance is his predation structure&#39;s form of &quot;monopolizing judgment right.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tang-Luo Weight Imbalance</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Weight Balance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One person judges</td><td>Anchor Council collectively legislates, weight allocated by seats</td></tr><tr><td>Consensus outsourced</td><td>Myriad Races republican co-construction, consensus negotiated by all beings</td></tr><tr><td>Single-polarized decisions</td><td>Four powers separated, any decision can be judicially reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Calibration missing</td><td>Anchor Supervision Committee calibrates all powers</td></tr><tr><td>Weight solidified</td><td>Anchor structure multi-layer redundant, weight distributed on network</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: turn &quot;Tang Luo&#39;s judgment&quot; into &quot;network consensus.&quot; Weight is not zero-sum, but distributed glowing.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Tang-Luo weight distribution, marking personal weight proportion</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Group A personal weight 90%+; Group B distributed weight</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: decision error rate, consensus-forming speed</li><li><strong>Review expectation</strong>: Group A error rate high and cannot self-correct; Group B error rate low and auto-calibrated</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-high</strong>. Protagonist weight high is web-novel convention</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong>. Long-form late if it needs &quot;Tang Luo errs&quot; to create turns, the early &quot;Tang Luo is always right&quot; setting is torn</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: a billion heads&#39; wisdom compressed into one person&#39;s judgment</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: monopolizing judgment right = preying on all beings&#39; right to think</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s weight too high is precisely his system&#39;s soft underbelly</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: distributed weight can cover 99%</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane governance must be distributed-decision</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-discussion-recalibration-of-civilization-weight" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Discussion: Recalibration of Civilization Weight <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-discussion-recalibration-of-civilization-weight" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Discussion: Recalibration of Civilization Weight&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang Luo&#39;s personal weight and civilization consensus imbalance is the bestowal-style civilization&#39;s structural problem. Heng Yuan Zhou through the Alaya Network&#39;s civilization-weight auto-evaluation system, quantitatively benchmarks personal contribution and civilization consensus. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization does not deny strong ones&#39; value, but the law-first axiom requires strong ones&#39; weight to match institutional construction — no matter how good personal conduct is, if institutional construction lags, civilization weight cannot rise. The universal equal infinite law ensures civilization weight does not over-tilt toward any single individual; 99% of Myriad-Races participants together form the weight&#39;s subject.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilization weight cannot be pressed too heavily on one person. Tang Luo&#39;s greatness is precisely his system&#39;s fragility. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer: let weight be distributed among Myriad Races, let any one person — including Tang Luo himself — be only an ordinary node of civilization.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · civilization weight analysis described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./20-锚点结构与层级.html">20-Anchor Structure and Hierarchy</a> · <a href="./29-共生度评估体系.html">29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System</a> · <a href="./49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">49-Governance Framework and Power Checks</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const m=e(s,[["render",a]]);export{d as __pageData,m as default};
